Got it. I'll keep every raw timing sample, not just a summary, and for each workload report:
- mean ± stddev and median;
- spread (min, p5/p95, MAD) and the share of outliers;
- the shape of the distribution: skewness, a normal vs log-normal fit, and histograms.

